Description: I2P Testnet Emulator - Cyber Warfare Research Platform
 A controlled desktop I2P testnet emulator for isolated deployment,
 monitoring, measurement, churn testing, topology analysis, and
 authoritative exact-hop validation.
 .
 Designed for cybersecurity researchers, law enforcement training, and
 national security exercises. Provides a safe, isolated environment to
 study how the Invisible Internet Project (I2P) operates — including
 covert communication layers, command-and-control infrastructure, and
 darknet eepsite behaviour — without touching live I2P infrastructure.
 .
 Features:
  - Isolated I2P routers in Linux network namespaces
  - Configurable multi-country topology with public-style IP emulation
  - GUI-based deployment, churn testing, and measurement campaigns
  - Phase 5 authoritative exact-hop truth pipeline
  - Exportable datasets for academic and forensic reporting
